%% Mermaid sequence diagram: Residency & Policy Enforcement v1
sequenceDiagram
  participant Org as Org Admin
  participant Settings as Settings Service
  participant LPE as LPE Compiler
  participant Bundles as OPA Bundle Store
  participant OPA as Service OPA Sidecar
  participant Worker as Worker (Celery/HTTP)
  participant Guardian as Guardian
  participant Portal as Portal Client/API

  Org->>Settings: Submit residency/settings activation (HMAC + approvals)
  Settings->>LPE: Trigger compile (policy context + region catalog)
  LPE->>Bundles: Publish signed discovery manifest & bundles
  Bundles-->>OPA: Hot-reload signed bundle (digest verified)
  Worker->>LPE: Fetch PolicyContext (digest, masking_profile, allowlists)
  Worker->>OPA: Evaluate residency allow for job (org, case, artifact)
  OPA-->>Worker: allow=false? reason=REGION_NOT_ALLOWED
  Worker-->>Guardian: Submit artifact + context digest (+ waiver_id?)
  Guardian->>OPA: Re-evaluate residency/waiver policy
  OPA-->>Guardian: Decision allow or block with reason code
  Guardian-->>Worker: READY or QUARANTINED (+ reason codes)
  Portal->>Guardian: Request artifact download (signed URL)
  Guardian->>OPA: Fetch-time residency check using latest PolicyContext
  OPA-->>Guardian: allow or block (reason, waiver reference)
  Guardian-->>Portal: Allow download (signed URL) / POLICY_BLOCK

  alt Residency waiver active
    Org->>Settings: Record waiver (App.O) with expiry & approvals
    Settings->>LPE: Compile waiver flag into PolicyContext
    Guardian->>OPA: Evaluate with waiver; stamp manifest `cross_region=true`
  end
